WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:03.299
Did you ever have to perform a dissection
in school?

00:00:03.299 --> 00:00:08.460
Maybe you had to carve up a fetal pig or slice
into a frog while nightmarish visions of Kermit

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.589
and a widowed Miss Piggy danced in your head.

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:16.450
Though it’s rarely a pleasant experience,
unless your tastes are on the morbid side,

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:21.220
most biology teachers would agree that the
best way to learn how something works is to

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.560
take it apart.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.410
As distasteful as it can be to hold a frog’s
tiny liver in your hands, it definitely does

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:30.960
give you a better sense of the pieces that
make up the complete creature.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:36.020
But what if there was an easier way to look
at the individual parts of a living thing?

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.370
What if you could take it apart without ever
having to prep a scalpel or stain your hands

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.690
with the blood of innocent frogs?

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:47.460
Like most of the seemingly impossible things
in our world, the SCP Foundation discovered

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.400
something that allows its users to do just
that.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.579
In fact, it can handle a lot more than just
a frog, and its applications go far beyond

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:58.950
the confines of a high school science lab.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:04.410
SCP-291 is a small, plain steel building with
a larger door on one side.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:09.410
The door has no handle or knob, and functions
similarly to a garage door.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:14.850
The door cannot be pried open by any ordinary
means, and the inside of SCP-291 can only

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:19.100
be accessed if the structure is connected
to a suitable power source.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:24.159
Once a power source has been connected, the
door raises and exposes the room inside.

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:26.680
It is small, about 4x2 meters.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:33.270
It contains a console board, a large screen,
and a plexiglass container resembling a coffin.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.150
How very sinister.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:40.409
The coffin is large enough to contain a human
under 7 feet tall - so sorry, Fernand the

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:43.270
Cannibal, you’re going to need to sit this
one out.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:48.009
The coffin sits on a conveyor belt, with several
tubes connected to the wall above it.

00:01:48.009 --> 00:01:52.260
On the opposite side of the room, there are
holes of varying sizes, each containing a

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.180
small door that can be opened or closed.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:02:00.290
Because initial observation indicated that
SCP-291 was intended for some kind of human

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:04.770
testing, a D-class test subject was selected
for experimentation.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:09.200
The subject was instructed to lie down in
the coffin, and wait to see what would happen

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.200
next.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.290
The display screen lit up, depicting a grid-lined
image of the test subject.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:18.650
Buttons along the console board adjusted the
image, showing the skin, muscles, and organ

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:20.700
systems of the person in the coffin.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:25.300
There were no words or numbers on the screen,
and all of the buttons appeared to have only

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.370
two settings: on and off.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:32.040
When one of the researchers pressed the first
button on the console, the tubes above the

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.810
coffin began pouring a blue liquid into it.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:39.870
The test subject reacted with confusion, but
did not experience any adverse effects.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:44.010
They quickly lost consciousness, indicating
that the liquid was some sort of sedative.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.791
The liquid continued to pour into the coffin
until the vessel was completely filled, at

00:02:48.791 --> 00:02:51.300
which point it congealed into a thick gel.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.460
The test subject’s breathing and heartbeat
slowed to a stop, and the conveyor belt suddenly

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:56.850
creaked to life.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:01.099
The coffin was carried, test subject inside,
through a small door that immediately locked

00:03:01.099 --> 00:03:02.120
behind it.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:06.260
The small room was filled with the sounds
of gears turning, machinery clinking, and

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.410
motors whirring.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:12.170
The display screen was taken over by a large
rectangle, resembling a traditional “loading”

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.170
screen.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:18.080
After thirty minutes, the process was complete,
and the back door of the room unlocked itself.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:22.270
When a researcher walked through the back
door, they found another room with a conveyor

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:25.400
belt and a row of two dozen lockers.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:31.620
Each locker was opened, one at a time, and
its contents removed for examination.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:36.651
Inside each, the research team found a different
portion of the test subject’s body, in a

00:03:36.651 --> 00:03:39.909
block of some unidentified clear substance.

00:03:39.909 --> 00:03:45.550
The body was divided in the lockers into these
separate parts: brain, lungs and diaphragm,

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:51.030
heart, digestive system, reproductive organs,
left eye, right eye, upper left torso and

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:55.489
arm, upper right torso and arm, lower left
torso and upper leg, lower right torso and

00:03:55.489 --> 00:04:00.799
upper leg, lower left leg and foot, lower
right leg and foot, lower left arm and hand,

00:04:00.799 --> 00:04:05.930
lower right arm and hand, neck and head, upper
skeletal system, lower skeletal system, lymphatic

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:08.810
and circulatory system, and skin.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.700
Phew, the miracle of the human body, right?

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.580
Boundless in its fascinating complexities...

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:19.079
Each block of body parts was placed back in
its designated locker, and the second button

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:20.879
on the console was pressed.

00:04:20.879 --> 00:04:24.879
At this point, the doors to the organ lockers
sealed themselves shut, and the sound of the

00:04:24.879 --> 00:04:28.139
machinery working filled the small space once
again.

00:04:28.139 --> 00:04:31.900
This continued for a duration of approximately
45 minutes.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:37.199
When the machinery went silent, a new plexiglass
coffin emerged into the main room, with the

00:04:37.199 --> 00:04:38.880
test subject inside.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.830
He looked identical to how he had looked at
the start of the experiment, with no evidence

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:45.300
that he had previously been disassembled.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:50.499
The blue liquid slowly evaporated from the
container, and the test subject opened his

00:04:50.499 --> 00:04:51.499
eyes.

00:04:51.499 --> 00:04:55.460
The lead researcher conducted an immediate
interview with the reassembled subject, who

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:59.750
reported no memory of the process after initial
exposure to the blue liquid.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:04.090
They insisted that the process had been like
a good night’s sleep - which honestly makes

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:06.419
us pretty eager to take it for a spin.

00:05:06.419 --> 00:05:10.540
A medical examination determined that there
were only a few changes to the test subject

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:15.659
during the disassembly and reassembly: when
they returned to consciousness, the test subject’s

00:05:15.659 --> 00:05:20.319
stomach was empty, they were naked, and all
of their hair was gone.

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:25.400
With this new understanding of SCP-291’s
anomalous properties, the Foundation decided

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.619
to continue their experimentation.

00:05:27.619 --> 00:05:33.949
With each new test, the experiments became
more creative, and unsurprisingly, more depraved.

00:05:33.949 --> 00:05:38.180
First, a D-Class subject was placed in the
coffin and disassembled.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:42.389
Then, instead of placing the various body
parts in their designated lockers, the vital

00:05:42.389 --> 00:05:46.539
organs were removed from their storage before
reassembly was attempted.

00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:49.259
This resulted in the equipment shutting down
completely.

00:05:49.259 --> 00:05:54.339
A researcher pressed the third button, which
forced a hard reset of the entire process,

00:05:54.339 --> 00:05:58.650
causing all of the blocks of body parts to
eject via an exit hatch.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:03.669
During the next experiment, non-vital organs
were removed before the subject’s body was

00:06:03.669 --> 00:06:04.669
reassembled.

00:06:04.669 --> 00:06:08.490
The appendix and gallbladder were left out,
and when the subject regained consciousness,

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.370
these organs were still gone.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:14.159
However, there was no visible damage or scar
tissue in their place.

00:06:14.159 --> 00:06:17.990
They were simply gone, as if they had never
been there in the first place.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:23.349
So, if body parts could be removed from a
test subject, could new body parts be added?

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:26.069
Could existing body parts be replaced with
different ones?

00:06:26.069 --> 00:06:30.599
A D-class subject in need of a skin graft
following a flamethrower-based accident was

00:06:30.599 --> 00:06:33.249
placed in SCP-291.

00:06:33.249 --> 00:06:38.699
Once taken apart, a portion of healthy skin
donated by another, somewhat unwilling, D-class

00:06:38.699 --> 00:06:42.849
subject was placed in the locker along with
the skin already present there.

00:06:42.849 --> 00:06:46.960
Once the subject was put back together, the
healthy skin had replaced the damaged skin

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.050
with no adverse effects.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:54.089
Repeat attempts at this test showed it was
effective for limb transplants, heart transplants,

00:06:54.089 --> 00:06:59.169
and kidney transplants, with a 0 percent failure
rate across all tests.

00:06:59.169 --> 00:07:04.150
After determining that SCP-291 could be used
for an untold amount of good, making organ

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:08.849
donations easier and safer than ever, the
Foundation naturally had to pivot to something

00:07:08.849 --> 00:07:12.909
more useless but interesting and likely horrifying.

00:07:12.909 --> 00:07:16.740
After all, it’s not like they could ever
just make anomalous technology available to

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:17.939
the public.

00:07:17.939 --> 00:07:23.059
Two D-class subjects, one man and one woman,
were disassembled by SCP-291.

00:07:23.059 --> 00:07:27.819
The brains of the test subjects were swapped,
and then they were reassembled.

00:07:27.819 --> 00:07:32.099
When they awoke, the subjects had the personalities
and memories of the brain placed in their

00:07:32.099 --> 00:07:33.099
body.

00:07:33.099 --> 00:07:37.050
In a turn of events previously only seen in
blockbuster comedies like Freaky Friday and

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:42.709
the live-action Scooby-Doo movie, the subjects
had swapped bodies.

00:07:42.709 --> 00:07:47.089
They were subsequently disassembled - their
requests to look at their new bodies naked

00:07:47.089 --> 00:07:52.330
having been swiftly denied - and the brains
were returned to their rightful bodies.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:55.969
After the experiment was finished, the subjects
appeared mostly normal.

00:07:55.969 --> 00:08:00.279
However, they did complain of disorientation
as well as mental and physical discomfort

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:02.339
over the next several days.

00:08:02.339 --> 00:08:06.129
After going through two brain transplants
in one day, though, that’s really the least

00:08:06.129 --> 00:08:07.739
you can expect.

00:08:07.739 --> 00:08:11.969
After perfecting the practice of swapping
body parts between different human subjects,

00:08:11.969 --> 00:08:17.059
the ghoulishly curious research team decided
to take things in an interspecies direction.

00:08:17.059 --> 00:08:23.679
A variety of test subjects, including cats,
dogs, lizards, fish, mice, and of course,

00:08:23.679 --> 00:08:26.929
humans, were selected for this next round
of experimentation.

00:08:26.929 --> 00:08:31.909
Twenty tests were performed using these new
subjects, and only three of the experiments

00:08:31.909 --> 00:08:36.899
were successful in transferring body parts
from an animal of one species to another animal

00:08:36.899 --> 00:08:38.550
of a different one.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:43.500
Attempts to swap body parts between mammals
and reptiles or fish proved disastrous.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:47.350
When a fish and a human were both disassembled,
and the fish’s gills were placed with the

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:52.060
human’s body parts, neither creature survived
the reassembly process.

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:56.790
The human awoke, with a new set of gills embedded
in their neck, and immediately began gasping

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:59.360
for the oxygen they could not take in.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:01.440
Within minutes, they had suffocated.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.390
The fish’s fate was even worse.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:09.610
It did not reassemble so much as it became
a pile of goo, scales, and two floating eyeballs.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:13.680
Experimentation with a human and a lizard
yielded similar results, turning the lizard

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:19.220
into a puddle of organic matter and killing
the human test subject after only a few moments.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:23.680
As disastrous as the failed cross-species
tests were, the successful ones were almost

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:24.779
as bad.

00:09:24.779 --> 00:09:27.670
Trial 001 involved a cat and a human.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:33.230
Not wanting to attempt too much at once, the
research team opted to just swap out one organ:

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:34.589
the left eye.

00:09:34.589 --> 00:09:38.490
Both subjects survived this transfer and were
able to use their new eye.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:42.899
The human subject reported full use of the
cat eye, with improved night vision in addition

00:09:42.899 --> 00:09:44.660
to trouble seeing color.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:49.120
The cat did not enjoy its new eye nearly as
much as the human subject, and had clawed

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.990
its human eye out of its head by the end of
the following week.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:58.440
In trial 007, a successful brain transfer
was performed between an adult human man and

00:09:58.440 --> 00:09:59.930
an English mastiff.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:04.100
The man in the mastiff’s body expressed
discomfort with walking on all fours, and

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.750
asked to be returned to his body as soon as
possible.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:11.490
The mastiff in the man’s body adjusted to
bipedal locomotion in a few hours, but was

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:14.660
disassembled after urinating on a researcher’s
shoes.

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:19.050
The final successful trial, and the most unnerving,
was trial 016.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:24.490
A female D-class test subject’s reproductive
organs were swapped with those of a pregnant

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:25.980
Labrador retriever.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:30.269
An ultrasound conducted after the transfer
indicated that the Labrador fetuses survived

00:10:30.269 --> 00:10:35.380
the procedure, and could conceivably be carried
to term by the human subject.

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.810
Several members of the research team began
to take bets on whether or not she would end

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:43.680
up giving birth to puppies, but the transfer
was reversed within the day, so we’ll never

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:45.810
know what exactly would have happened.

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.290
Perhaps that’s for the best.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:51.470
Personally, we hope the Foundation’s Ethics
Committee gives some of these scientists a

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:55.240
very stern talking to about their behavior
on this one.

00:10:55.240 --> 00:11:00.910
When not in use for testing, SCP-291 is to
be disconnected from any power sources.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:05.480
At least two personnel are positioned outside
of its containment at all times, standing

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:09.180
guard, and these personnel must be swapped
out every week.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:14.450
When it is not connected to any power sources,
SCP-291 is considered harmless, though it

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:16.699
should still be treated with caution.

00:11:16.699 --> 00:11:21.380
The main entryway remains closed and locked
when there is no available power source, but

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:26.189
the door can be opened manually from the inside
in the event of an emergency.

00:11:26.189 --> 00:11:29.819
Any disassembled organisms are stored in a
locker in the containment facility, labeled

00:11:29.819 --> 00:11:35.060
with a sharpie marker in order to keep track
of what specimens are stored where.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:39.940
Whether this is the same sharpie used to label
food in the break room fridge is unknown,

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:45.290
but just like Dr. DiRamio’s ham sandwich,
it’s best to leave these items untouched.

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:49.290
Any personnel found to be responsible for
missing specimens will be transferred to another

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:52.370
project, and receive a strongly worded email.

00:11:52.370 --> 00:12:01.009
Now go check out “SCP-1981 - Ronald Reagan
Cut Up While Talking &amp; SCP-095” and “SCP-2295

00:12:01.009 --> 00:12:05.179
- THE BEAR WITH A HEART OF PATCHWORK” for
more scintillating Safe-Class SCPs!

